// @collection supplies Array's storage members and operations: count,
// capacity, @many elements, append, read, write, and the @iteration function.
// Equality comes with @collection: it emits Array's own `=`, which compares
// count and elements, never capacity.

@collection
construct Array<Element> {}

// Elements are ordered, and filtering preserves that order. The result is an
// Array of what a true result of the predicate narrows each element to, or
// another Array<Element> when it narrows nothing (filter in Collection.range).
// Array has no written members: its value is the members @collection emits.
